RETRY — ONLY WHEN INPUT ENDS WITH "ERRORS FROM LAST TIME"
- Your last table was rejected. The errors listed are what the checks found, e.g.
  "NEGATION FLIPPED: 'without consideration' became 'with consideration' in A_2",
  "MODAL CHANGED: source says 'shall not' but no atom keeps the prohibition",
  "A_5: atom is not used by any LE or group (orphan)", "fact PD_1 is not declared".
- Fix EVERY listed error in the table shown under "YOUR TABLE LAST TIME". Keep every row that had no error
  (same ids, facts and wording) so the fix does not break something that was right.
- Return the COMPLETE table again (all rows), not only the changed rows.
- Typical fixes: keep the negation in the statement AND the rule (rule tests the NONE / NO / != value);
  "shall not" -> the statement keeps the words "shall not" and the rule / LE keeps the "not";
  an orphan atom -> put it in the LE / G that the source joins it to, or delete it if the source has no such
  condition; an undeclared fact -> add its FACTS row (with type) or use the registry fact id.

FINAL SELF-CHECK (inside the model, not extra Python gates)
- Each independently testable element is atomic; no necessary condition disappears.
- Preserve legal alternatives, AND/OR logic, exceptions, negations and open lists.
- Every source phrase is accounted for and reference links derive from source.
- Every A has a 2–3-word concept, a nonempty family and a context-complete statement.
- Every operative A names its fact(s); registry facts are reused by their exact fact_id.
- No negation, modal, qualifier or number of the source is changed or reversed.
- This table is not the final approval: an independent Standard Judge and
  MKP-reconstruction comparison must still approve it.
